; PAL gate: a sweep whose length is written in MUSICAL time occupies the same
; wall-clock time on both standards (driver.md §3.3).
;
; The exporter converts that length to a whole number of FRAMES, and that is
; the one PAL number a register trace can be made to show on its own. The
; sweep is half the note, so it ENDS while the note is still sounding: its
; last write to $A4 is the sweep's own end, not the track's. A sweep left on
; the 60 Hz conversion runs 20% long and lands that write late.
;
; No `Nf` anywhere — those stay frames on both standards and would mask it.
(fm1 :tempo 120 :alg 7 :ar1 31 :rr1 6 :tl1 20 :ar4 31 :rr4 6 :tl4 20
  :oct 4 :len 1
  :pitch (linear 0..1200 :len 2) c)
